Build-time and shipped media components
---------------------------------------

The Windows release includes a statically built FFmpeg sidecar. Its configure
uses `--enable-gpl --enable-version3`, so that binary is GPL-3.0-or-later.
The source is FFmpeg 8.1 from https://ffmpeg.org/releases/ffmpeg-8.1.tar.xz,
with the build configuration recorded in `.github/workflows/release.yml`,
`windows-msix.yml` and the development workflow.

| Component | Version / origin | Licence | Notes |
|---|---|---|---|
| FFmpeg | 8.1 | GPL-3.0-or-later for the shipped sidecar; LGPL/GPL upstream | Configure flags choose the GPLv3 build. |
| x264 | upstream `videolan/x264` | GPL-2.0-or-later | Source headers state "version 2 or later"; commercial terms also offered upstream. Build commit is not pinned. |
| x265 | upstream `multicoreware/x265_git` | GPL-2.0-or-later | Source headers state "version 2 or later"; commercial terms also offered upstream. The `.pc` says 4.1.0, but the build clones without checking out that tag. |
| libdvdread | 6.1.3 | GPL-2.0-or-later | DVD-Video reading. |
| libdvdnav | 6.1.1 | GPL-2.0-or-later | DVD-Video navigation. |
| FreeType | 2.13.3 | FTL / GPL-2.0-only | Font rasterisation. |
| HarfBuzz | 14.4.0 | MIT | Text shaping. |

The static FFmpeg build also links transitive libraries supplied by the build
environment. Their notices remain with those projects. The build scripts record
the configured versions but are not a complete transitive-licence inventory.

